Z||000004||beer_stud_21||08-08-2001||12:13 AM||||Now you need to do the TB coolant bypass mod.  1st2m6 gave me the instructions at one point.  Very easy.  I can't say if there was any performance improvement in my case because A) I never drove my car with the TB coolant lines hooked up and B) I have yet to really drive it with then disconnected.  But it does really clean up the engine compartment and makes it MUCH MUCH easier to get at the coil and distributor.  If you want the instructions travis gave me let me know and I will find them and repost them here.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroMaster88||08-08-2001||12:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by beer_stud_21:<BR><B>Now you need to do the TB coolant bypass mod.  1st2m6 gave me the instructions at one point.  Very easy.  I can't say if there was any performance improvement in my case because A) I never drove my car with the TB coolant lines hooked up and B) I have yet to really drive it with then disconnected.  But it does really clean up the engine compartment and makes it MUCH MUCH easier to get at the coil and distributor.  If you want the instructions travis gave me let me know and I will find them and repost them here.<P>-Marlin</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sure man...shoot them this way!  I always need something to do in my spare time.  What else can I do as far as mods go?  Looking for some "cheaper" things to do until this winter when my car goes away into storage.<P><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
