Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||08-08-2001||10:04 AM||||BeerStud... I'd like to see the info on the TB coolant bypass- got any pics?<P>FieroMaster88...nice ride-I like the aircleaner mounting. What parts did you use for that?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000008||88CoupeV6||08-08-2001||10:22 AM||||Looks sweet, Do you have binding problems with the shift cables under the intake tube? I ran mine over the top because I thought it would put too much stress on them going under.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lucky1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||5
Z||000009||FieroMaster88||08-08-2001||01:19 PM||||The air cleaner is the factory air canaster with the center cut out......and the intake tube connected to the end.  <P>The shift cables have not given me any problems being routed liek that.  I was afraid they were gonna melt when i had them go over the intake pipe because that put them closer to the exhaust manafold.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000010||beer_stud_21||08-08-2001||01:23 PM||||Here is travis's message in its entirty.  I can get you a pic but not yet, Im real busy today and about to head out for most of the day.  Ill try to put one up tonight.<P>"how to...<P>make sure you do with with the car STONE COLD! <P>ok here we go.. - remove the intake tube and unscrew the 12mm compression fittings on the TB. some coolant will drain out. once both lines have been un screwed from the TB. you'll see a 12point 7mm bolt on the left side of the intake pelenum. remove this shiney bolt and the hose should drop a bit. on the right side of the intake you'll see the MAP sensor.. unplug it and try not to break the hard plastic vacuum lines running to it. once this has been done you'll see a 10mm black screw that goes through the back of the MAP sensor braket into the intake pelenum remove that 10mm screw. ok there is NOTHING holding the tubes now.. remove the passengerside battery cover/grill vent. trace the hard pipes to the soft tubing at the thermostat housing.. remove both pliable hoses at the thermostat housing. the easiest way i've found to pull the hard pipes out is to cut them at the mount on the drivers side... if you just pull you may pull the vacuum line off the fuel pressure regulator. thats BAD! once you figured out the magic of hard pipe removal... take the clamps that were already on the stock soft hoses and cut a piece about 8" long. attach the NEW transmission/fuel/coolant hose to the 2 nipples that the factory tied into and just make a run from one to the other... make sure you tightend the hose clamps.. reinstall the MAP sensor, thats it... put the grill back on the car.. start it up and hose off the coolant fron the Y-pipe. WITH THE CAR RUNNING! and don't use a pressure washer... just running water.. if you do this with the car off and it don't start take the distributor cap off.. spray the inside with WD40 (it displaces the water) and reinstall.. it'll start now.. (old 4x4 trick)"<P>When I did it I took off the bracket that held the map sensor and cut off the part where the coolant lines attached.  Looks good that way.  very clean.  I used a crappy ass right angle grinder to do it.  <P>a pretty nice mod for less than 5 bucks.<P>-Marlin<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroMaster88||08-09-2001||01:59 PM||||Thanks for that info.  I will have to do that.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||4
